# Style for the endpoint's C (firmware/). Chosen by measurement, not taste:
# each candidate was run over every tracked firmware *.c/*.h with
# IndentWidth 4, ColumnLimit 100, BreakBeforeBraces Linux, PointerAlignment
# Right and SortIncludes Never (what the code already did by hand), and the
# one that changed the fewest lines won.
#
#   base        lines changed
#   Microsoft     428   (chosen)
#   LLVM          478   (428 with AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: None)
#   Google       1447
#   Chromium     1797
#   WebKit       2743
#   Mozilla      4237
#   GNU          7221
#
# Microsoft already has IndentWidth 4, PointerAlignment Right and short
# functions never on one line, so it needs the fewest overrides. ColumnLimit
# 90/95/98/104 all changed more than 100. SortIncludes stays Never: include
# order can matter under ESP-IDF, and sorting is not a formatter's call.
#
# clang-format 23.1.1, PyPI clang-format wheel,
# https://pypi.org/project/clang-format/ read 2026-09-30
BasedOnStyle: Microsoft
ColumnLimit: 100
BreakBeforeBraces: Linux
SortIncludes: Never
